198	  | `liveness n: [forall i in g:] eventually e [under fair {…}]` | `liveness('n', { eventually: ($) => e }, { forall?: ['i', 'g'], fair?: [[member, …], …] })`; `leads to` is `{ from: ($) => p, to: ($) => q }`; a member is `'A'` or `'A(*)'` |
199	  | `effect k(p: T) { items }` | `effect('k', { p: T }, [kind('…'), labels([…]), cls('…'), retry(n, '200ms', '5s'), ok('A', args), failed('A', args), exhausted('A', args)])` |
200	  | a name `x` (field, parameter, local, constructor, `none`, `self`, `pre`, `post`, `action`) | `$.x`, a property of the arrow's one parameter |
201	  | `e.f` | `e.f` on any expression other than `$` itself |
202	  | `e[k]`, `g[*]` | `e[k]`, `$.g[ALL]` |
203	  | literals | number, `true`, `false`, a string literal |
204	  | `==`, `!=`, `&&`, `\|\|`, `!`, `-`, `+`, `*`, `/`, `%`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` | `===`, `!==`, and the operator itself |
205	  | `a implies b`, `e is C1 \| C2`, `e in { a, b }` | `implies(a, b)`, `is(e, 'C1', 'C2')`, `isIn(e, [a, b])` |
206	  | `C { p: e }`, `T.C { p: e }` | `ctor('C', { p: e })`, `ctor('T.C', { p: e })` |
207	  | `{ k: v, … }` (a map or a record) | an object literal: an identifier key is a name, a numeric key an int, a string key a string, and `[e]: v` any other key; as an operand of an operator it is `lit({ … })`, since tsc refuses `===` with an object literal (S84) |
208	  | `[v0, …]` | an array literal |
209	  | `count`, `before`, `rejected`, `init`, `sum`, `all`, `any` | the function of that name |
210	  | `k spawned`, `f[i] spawned` | `spawned($.k)`, `spawned($.f[i])` |
211	  | `forall i in g: e`, `exists …` | `forall('i', 'g', ($) => e)`, `exists(…)` |
